      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T16:14:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another interesting discussion point in section 21.14 (Rapid Commit Option):\n\n      The problem of unused leases can be minimized by designing the\n      DHCP service so that only one server responds to the Solicit or by\n      using relatively short lifetimes for newly assigned leases.\n\nSo rejecting short-lived leases might not be a good option after all as an initial lease might be much shorter than the subsequent ones.\n\nLet\u0027s keep thinking about this some more.",
      "parentUuid": "ee7dedb6_294fb34f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "b5be47841750be3fecb71f380141b632480a65ad",
